  "issue": {
    "body": "As we do in other encode projects, we should run mypy against our test code to make sure the type annotations in the project work well when the project is actually used.\r\n\r\nWe do this not by adding type annotations to all the tests (as this is often not very useful for test code) but rather by using mypy's `check_untyped_defs` option. We usually have a mypy config like:\r\n\r\n```ini\r\n[mypy]\r\ndisallow_untyped_defs = True\r\nignore_missing_imports = True\r\n\r\n[mypy-tests.*]\r\ndisallow_untyped_defs = False\r\ncheck_untyped_defs = True\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs of writing, enabling `check_untyped_defs` for the tests directory results in a lot of mypy errors which need to be fixed.",
    "body_last_edited_at": "2020-09-06T09:33:49Z",
    "closed_at": "2022-01-11T08:28:39Z",
    "created_at": "2020-09-06T09:32:21Z",
